 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518437,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "How much must be deposited per quarter in an account bearing 2.98% interest compounded quarterly if the account is to be worth $300,000 after 25 years?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$2,030.65"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>To compute the payment to reach a final goal, the payment (<i>pmt</i>) of an ordinary annuity to reach a specific future value (<i>FV</i>) is <span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{FV \\times \\frac{r}{n}}}{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}} - 1}}\"></span>, where <i>r</i> is the annual interest rate (in decimal form), <i>n</i> is the number of compounding periods per year, and <i>t</i> is the number of years. Round up!</p>\n<p>Once again, it will help you get the right answer using your calculator to find <span data-math=\"n \\times t\"></span> first.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n \\times t = \\left( 4 \\right)\\left( {25} \\right) = 100\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{\\left( {300,000 \\times \\frac{{0.0298}}{4}} \\right)}}{{\\left( {{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.0298}}{4}} \\right)}^{100}} - 1} \\right)}} = \\$2,030.65\"></span></p>\n<p>Additional parentheses were added to help you enter the expression properly in your calculator.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
